                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "-intercept: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(8\\sqrt2-4,0)\\approx(7.31,0)",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p42-q8-c-answer-y",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "-intercept: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(0,-1.5)",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For the $x$-intercept, let $y=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}0&=\\log_2(x+4)-\\frac72\\\\\\log_2(x+4)&=\\frac72\\\\x+4&=2^{7/2}\\\\x&=8\\sqrt2-4\\\\x&\\approx7.31\\end{align*}$$\nFor the $y$-intercept, let $x=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\log_2(0+4)-\\frac72\\\\y&=2-\\frac72\\\\y&=-\\frac32=-1.5\\end{align*}$$\nThe intercepts are $(8\\sqrt2-4,0)\\approx(7.31,0)$ and $(0,-1.5)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "State the horizontal and vertical translations applied to the graph of $\\log_2 x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Left by 4, down by 3.5.",
          "worked": "Replacing $x$ with $x+4$ translates the graph 4 units left. Subtracting 3.5 translates it 3.5 units down.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      }
